Round 1 (2026-02-26)

What changed
- File changed: clang/aot/emit.c.
- Added a conservative DUP fast-path in the AOT emitter for both head mode and expression mode.
- New rule: only compile through DUP when the DUP value subtree is statically copy-free (NUM/C00/constructor tree of those).
- Added helper:
  - aot_emit_is_static_copy_free_rec(loc, fuel)
  - aot_emit_is_static_copy_free(loc)
- Fuel limit is 1024 to avoid emitter recursion overflow.

Important bug found and fixed
- Without fuel, compiling some benchmark files (ex: ../bench/bench/gab_deriv/main.hvm with -o) could segfault (exit 139) during AOT emission.
- Root cause: unbounded recursion in static copy-free check.
- Fix: fuel parameter and fail-closed when exhausted.

Failed approaches this round (reverted)
- Tried non-head APP-LAM inlining for LET-shaped terms.
- Tried expression-mode static constructor passthrough (C01..C16 -> heap_read when copy-free).
- These introduced benchmark/runtime regressions (notably gen_easy produced "RUNTIME_ERROR: cannot apply a number").
- Both were removed to restore correctness.

Validation done
- Rebuilt clang/main.
- Full suite passed twice:
  - ./test/_all_.sh
- Bench sanity checks (manual, benchmark-style flags):
  - gab_deriv: hvmi vs hvmc output matched.
  - gen_easy (-C1): hvmi vs hvmc output matched.
  - gen_hard (-C1): compiled binary runs and times out under short alarm (expected for small timeout).
- During bench.ts run, early hvmc ERROR rows were traced to intermediate buggy emitter state; after rollback/fixes those manual reproductions no longer error.

Useful operational notes
- bench.ts adds -C1 for gen_* benchmarks.
- Running multiple "--as-c" invocations in parallel collides on deterministic temp file paths; run sequentially.

Current state
- Conservative correctness-only DUP improvement is in place.
- No broad AOT speedup yet from this patch; it is mostly enabling a safe subset and avoiding previous regressions.

Next likely step
- If we want meaningful DUP coverage, implement explicit DUP binder state in fallback environments (pending dup cell vs substituted var), instead of forcing fallback for non-static DUP values.
